Subject: [PATCH] SDL: on KMSDRM, the gamepad drives a drawn cursor in menus

Under KMSDRM there is no window system, and on displays without a cursor
plane (e.g. sun4i-drm on the Allwinner A33) SDL can't show a cursor at
all. 5.17 plays well with a gamepad, but menus and the inventory still
need a mouse.

So when SDL's video driver is kmsdrm, while the cursor is visible (a
menu or formspec is open):
- either stick moves the cursor, the D-pad nudges it;
- A and Y are a left click, X a right click (take half a stack);
- B and START are Escape (close the menu, the inventory, the pause
  menu);
- L1/R1 are the mouse wheel.
The GUI environment then draws an arrow at the cursor at the end of
drawAll(). Buttons pressed as the mouse are released as the mouse too,
so the game never sees half a press. In game (cursor hidden) nothing
changes, and other video drivers are untouched.

Upstream: not sent; luanti-org/luanti#17341 (WIP) moves the focus with
the D-pad instead, with no answer for inventory lists yet.
---
